WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.993
Most of the reasoning in this module transfers to
other database systems

00:00:05.722 --> 00:00:09.974
AND OR NOT IS NULL coalesce null if and case are
widely

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.110
supported concepts But some syntax varies across
database systems For

00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:21.702
example PostgreSQL supports IS DISTINCT FROM Other
database systems

00:00:21.728 --> 00:00:27.231
may handle null-safe comparison differently
PostgreSQL can subtract one date

00:00:27.257 --> 00:00:31.767
from another directly Another system may use a
function such as date

00:00:31.793 --> 00:00:36.522
diff So when you move from PostgreSQL to another
database keep the

00:00:36.548 --> 00:00:40.362
logical rule the same but check whether any syntax
needs to change

00:00:41.264 --> 00:00:45.233
The best skill to carry between systems is not
memorizing every command

00:00:46.135 --> 00:00:49.112
It is being able to explain the rule clearly and
then translate

00:00:49.138 --> 00:00:51.290
that rule into the target SQL dialect
